"<p>Quick guide to the tabs on this page -- everything for looking a client (or their contacts/passwords) up by name.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Client Details</b> -- type a client name (wildcards with *, e.g. Acme*) to look up matching clients and their key details.</li>\n<li><b>Client Contacts</b> -- look up contacts across active clients, filterable to primary, billing, or all contacts.</li>\n<li><b>Client Activity</b> -- type a client name to see their ticket volume, logged hours, and open tickets over the last 12 months.</li>\n<li><b>Clients by Classification</b> -- active client counts by classification, shown as a bar chart. Click a bar to filter down to those clients.</li>\n<li><b>Find Passwords</b> -- search IT Glue password entries by name. Shows metadata only (which entry, which client) -- never the actual password.</li>\n</ul>"